gui_2c:'<span class="prompt-label">Prompt Example</span><span class="string">"당신은 반도체 후공정 품질 엔지니어입니다.</span><br><span class="string">&nbsp;다음 와이어 본딩 불량 데이터를 보고,</span><br><span class="string">&nbsp;단계별로 원인을 분석해주세요."</span>',
gui_3bg:"기법 ③",gui_3t:"출력 형식 지정",gui_3b:"추론 과정의 가독성을 높이려면 출력 형식까지 명시적으로 안내합니다.",
gui_3c:'<span class="prompt-label">Prompt Example</span><span class="string">"각 단계에 번호를 매기고, 단계마다 \'근거\'와 \'결론\'을</span><br><span class="string">&nbsp;구분해서 작성해주세요.</span><br><span class="string">&nbsp;마지막에 전체 요약을 3줄로 정리해주세요."</span>',
gui_4bg:"기법 ④",gui_4t:"자기 검증(Self-Verification) 추가",gui_4b:"추론 완료 후 모델이 자신의 답변을 되돌아보게 하면 한 단계 더 정확해집니다.",
gui_4c:'<span class="prompt-label">Prompt Example</span><span class="string">"답변을 완성한 후, 각 단계의 논리에 모순이 없는지</span><br><span class="string">&nbsp;스스로 검토하고, 오류가 있다면 수정해주세요."</span>',
gui_5bg:"기법 ⑤",gui_5t:"통합 적용 — L&D 실전 예시",gui_5b:"위 네 가지 기법(역할 부여 + 명확한 지시어 + 형식 지정 + 자기 검증)을 모두 결합한 프롬프트입니다. 반도체 후공정 L&D 업무에 바로 적용할 수 있는 형태를 보여줍니다.",
gui_5c:'<span class="prompt-label">Complete Prompt — 교육 모듈 설계 (Markdown 적용)</span><span class="md-h1"># 역할</span><br><span class="string">"당신은 반도체 후공정 교육 설계 전문가입니다."</span><br><br><span class="md-h2">## 과제</span><br><span class="string">"신입 엔지니어를 위한 \'솔더링 불량 유형과 대응\'</span><br><span class="string">&nbsp;교육 모듈을 설계해야 합니다."</span><br><br><span class="md-h2">## 단계</span><br><span class="comment">&nbsp;&nbsp;1단계 —</span> 솔더링 공정에서 발생하는 주요 불량 유형을 분류하세요.<br><span class="comment">&nbsp;&nbsp;2단계 —</span> 각 불량 유형의 기술적 원인을 분석하세요.<br><span class="comment">&nbsp;&nbsp;3단계 —</span> 각 원인에 대응하는 핵심 교육 포인트를 도출하세요.<br><span class="comment">&nbsp;&nbsp;4단계 —</span> 이를 90분 교육 세션 구조로 편성하세요.<br><span class="comment">&nbsp;&nbsp;5단계 —</span> 전체 흐름의 논리적 일관성을 검토하고, 필요시 수정하세요.<br><br><span class="md-h2">## 검증</span><br><span class="string">"마지막에 빠진 내용이나 논리적 비약이 없는지 확인해주세요."</span>',
cau_pill:"07 — 한계와 주의사항",cau_title:"만능키는 아닙니다.",cau_sub:"CoT는 강력한 기법이지만 만능이 아닙니다.<br>몇 가지 한계를 반드시 인지하고 사용해야 합니다.",
cau_1t:"잘못된 추론의 자기 강화",cau_1b:'중간 단계에서 오류가 발생하면, 모델은 그 오류를 전제로 이후 추론을 전개합니다. <strong style="color:var(--apple-gray-1);">(Confident Hallucination)</strong>이 생성될 수 있으므로 <strong style="color:var(--apple-gray-1);">반드시 사람의 검토가 수반</strong>되어야 합니다.',
cau_2t:"추론 ≠ 이해",cau_2b:'CoT로 생성된 단계별 설명이 모델의 진정한 "이해"를 의미하지는 않습니다. <strong style="color:var(--apple-gray-1);">도메인 전문가의 비판적 검토가 반드시 필요</strong>합니다.',
sum_pill:"08 — 핵심 요약",sum_title:"한눈에 보는 CoT.",sum_1l:"정의",sum_1b:"AI에게 결론까지의 중간 추론 과정을 단계별로 서술하도록 유도하는 프롬프팅 기법입니다.",sum_2l:"핵심 원리",sum_2b:"문제 분해 → 중간 결과의 맥락 전달 → 투명성·검증 가능성 확보",sum_rv:"복습하기",sum_3l:"주요 유형",
sum_quote:'"복잡한 문제에는 생각의 과정을 보여달라."',sum_close:"CoT는 결국 이 한 문장으로 요약됩니다.<br>다만 만능이 아니므로,<br>문제의 복잡도를 먼저 판단하고 적재적소에 적용하는 것이 진짜 실력입니다.<br>항상 사람의 검토를 병행하는 것을 잊지 마세요.",
ftr_title:"Chain of Thought 프롬프팅 핸드북 · AI로 일잘러 되기 시리즈 6",ftr_contact:"문의 사항 : L&D팀 정혁 수석"
},
en:{
nav_title:"CoT Handbook",nav_def:"Definition",nav_principle:"Principles",nav_comparison:"Comparison",nav_types:"Types",nav_usage:"Use Cases",nav_guide:"Guide",nav_caution:"Cautions",nav_summary:"Summary",
hero_series:"Work Smarter with AI — Series 6",hero_sub:"Chain of Thought",hero_tagline:'A technique that asks AI to show its "thinking process"',hero_team:"ATK L&D Team Prompting Handbook",hero_btn:"Get Started",
def_pill:"01 — Definition & Background",def_title:"What is<br>Chain of Thought?",def_subtitle:"A prompt engineering technique that guides AI models to explicitly describe intermediate reasoning steps toward a conclusion, rather than simply outputting the final answer.",
def_c1t:"Definition",
def_c1b:'Chain of Thought is a prompting technique that guides LLMs to explicitly generate intermediate reasoning steps, achieving both accuracy and transparency on complex problems. <span style="color:var(--apple-blue);font-weight:600;">The key is not just asking "tell me the answer," but demanding "show me how you arrived at that answer."</span>',
def_c2t:"Background",
def_c2b:'In 2022, Jason Wei et al. at Google Research formally proposed this in their paper <em>"Chain-of-Thought Prompting Elicits Reasoning in Large Language Models"</em> (NeurIPS 2022). <span style="color:var(--apple-blue);font-weight:600;">They demonstrated that simply including reasoning examples in prompts dramatically improved arithmetic, logical, and commonsense reasoning</span>, establishing CoT as a core prompt engineering technique.',
def_at:"Simple Analogy",
def_ab:'It\'s the same as requiring <strong style="color:var(--apple-gray-1);">"show your work"</strong> on a math exam. Writing only the answer makes it impossible to find mistakes—but showing your work reduces errors and enables verification. In semiconductor back-end terms, it\'s like <strong style="color:var(--apple-gray-1);">tracking yield at each process step</strong> rather than only looking at the final defect rate.',
pri_pill:"02 — Core Principles",pri_title:"Why Does It Work?",pri_sub:"CoT\'s effectiveness is explained by three core mechanisms.<br>Each principle combines organically to elevate the model\'s reasoning accuracy.",
pri_f1:"① Decomposition",pri_f2:"② Context Passing",pri_f3:"③ Transparency",pri_f4:"Accurate Conclusion",
pri_1t:"Problem Decomposition",pri_1b:'Breaks a complex problem into manageable sub-steps. <span style="color:#d1ff26;font-weight:500;">Since each step performs a small inference, the error probability at each step is significantly reduced.</span>',
pri_2t:"Intermediate Context Passing",pri_2b:'Each reasoning step\'s output serves as context for the next step. <span style="color:#d1ff26;font-weight:500;">The model references its own prior conclusions as it develops its logic</span>, increasing overall coherence and consistency.',
pri_3t:"Transparency & Verifiability",pri_3b:'Since the reasoning process is explicitly written out, <span style="color:#d1ff26;font-weight:500;">users can follow the model\'s logic and identify exactly where errors occurred.</span> This is CoT\'s most practical benefit—enabling reliability assessment and error correction.',
cmp_pill:"03 — Standard vs. CoT",cmp_title:"Same Question,<br>Different Results.",cmp_sub:"Comparing the difference when applying standard prompting vs. CoT prompting to the same problem.",
cmp_el:"Example Problem",cmp_et:'"A warehouse had 48 semiconductor trays. 15 were shipped in the morning, 8 received in the afternoon,<br>and 3 scrapped due to defects. How many trays remain?"',
cmp_pl:"Prompt",cmp_sp:"Please solve the above problem.",cmp_rl:"AI Response",cmp_sr:'"38."',cmp_sn:"The basis for the answer is unknown, and if an error occurs, it\'s impossible to identify where it went wrong.",
cmp_pl2:"Prompt",cmp_cp:'Please solve the above problem <span class="highlight">step by step</span>.',cmp_rl2:"AI Response",
cmp_cr:'<span class="comment">① Initial stock:</span> 48<br><span class="comment">② After morning shipment:</span> 48 − 15 = <span class="highlight">33</span><br><span class="comment">③ After afternoon receipt:</span> 33 + 8 = <span class="highlight">41</span><br><span class="comment">④ After scrapping:</span> 41 − 3 = <span class="string">38</span>',
cmp_cn:"Each step\'s reasoning is explicit, enabling immediate identification and correction of errors.",
cmp_dt:"Key Difference",cmp_db:'Standard Prompting follows an <strong style="color:var(--apple-gray-1);">"Input → Answer"</strong> structure, while CoT follows an <strong style="color:var(--apple-gray-1);">"Input → Reasoning₁ → Reasoning₂ → … → Answer"</strong> structure. For multi-step reasoning problems, the accuracy gap is dramatic, and the greatest practical benefit is that result verifiability is secured.',
typ_pill:"04 — Main Types of CoT",typ_title:"Four Approaches.",typ_sub:"CoT is not a single technique—multiple variants exist that can be selected based on the situation.",
typ_zs_tag:"Instruction-based",typ_zs_b:'Induces reasoning using only trigger phrases like <strong style="color:var(--apple-gray-1);">"Let\'s think step by step"</strong> without any examples. Even a single instruction line significantly improves reasoning performance.',
typ_zs_ex:'<span class="ep-label">Prompt Example</span><span class="ep-string">"A Ball lift defect occurred in the wire bonding process.</span><br><span class="ep-string">&nbsp;Please analyze the possible causes.</span><br><span class="ep-highlight">&nbsp;Let\'s think step by step."</span>',
typ_fs_tag:"Example-based",typ_fs_b:'Provides <strong style="color:var(--apple-gray-1);">1–3 examples including reasoning processes</strong> in the prompt, guiding the model to learn the pattern and apply the same reasoning to new problems.',
typ_fs_ex:'<span class="ep-label">Prompt Example</span>Refer to the solving method below, and solve my problem the same way.<br><br><span class="ep-highlight">Example)</span><br><span class="ep-highlight">Q:</span> <span class="ep-string">A café has 23 apples. Used 20, bought 6. How many?</span><br><span class="ep-highlight">A:</span> 23-20=3. 3+6=<span class="ep-string">9</span> (Show the process like this)<br><br>---<br><span class="ep-highlight">Q:</span> <span class="ep-string">Warehouse has 48 trays. 15 shipped, 8 received, 3 scrapped. How many?</span><br><span class="ep-highlight">A:</span> (Model solves step by step: 48-15=33, 33+8=41, 41-3=<span class="ep-string">38</span>)',
typ_au_tag:"Auto-generated",typ_au_b:'The model <strong style="color:var(--apple-gray-1);">automatically generates</strong> reasoning chains for various problems, then reuses them as few-shot examples. Reduces manual effort.',
typ_au_ex:'<span class="ep-label">Prompt Example</span><span class="ep-string">"(Presenting 5 packaging defect cases) Analyze each of the 5 packaging defect types through root cause reasoning, </span><span style="color:#64d2ff;font-weight:600;">then apply the same analysis to the new defect case below</span><span class="ep-string">."</span><br><span class="ep-string">&nbsp;(Attach new defect case)</span>',
typ_sc_tag:"Majority Vote",typ_sc_b:'Generates <strong style="color:var(--apple-gray-1);">multiple different CoT paths</strong> for a single problem, then selects the most frequently derived answer as the final answer.',
typ_sc_ex:'<span class="ep-label">Prompt Example</span><span class="ep-string">"Analyze the cause of yield decline from 3 different perspectives,</span><br><span class="ep-highlight">&nbsp;each independently and step by step.</span><br><span class="ep-string">&nbsp;Then compile the common conclusions</span><br><span class="ep-string">&nbsp;as the final answer."</span>',
use_pill:"05 — Use Cases",use_title:"When to Use,<br>When Not To.",use_sub:"CoT is not a silver bullet. The key is applying it precisely based on problem complexity.",
use_gt:"High-Impact Areas",use_g1t:"Multi-step Arithmetic",use_g1b:"Describing intermediate steps significantly reduces errors in yield calculations, cost analysis, and process parameter optimization.",use_g2t:"Logical & Causal Analysis",use_g2b:"Particularly effective in tasks like Root Cause Analysis that track cause and effect.",use_g3t:"Complex Decision-Making",use_g3b:"Suitable for evaluating pros/cons of multiple alternatives step by step to derive the optimal solution.",use_g4t:"Code Debugging & Process Design",use_g4b:"Suitable for tasks where sequence matters, such as curriculum design and project planning.",
use_bt:"Not Suitable For",use_b1t:"Simple Fact Lookup",use_b1b:"Accuracy stays the same but tokens are wasted—inefficient.",use_b2t:"Creative Writing & Emotional Chat",use_b2b:"In areas where free thinking matters, CoT can actually constrain creativity.",use_b3t:"Simple Classification",use_b3b:"For simple classification with clear criteria, a concise prompt is more efficient.",
use_tl:"💡 Quick Decision Rule",use_tb:'<span style="color:#d1ff26;font-weight:600;">"Does solving this problem require 2+ steps of thinking?"</span><br>→ <strong style="color:#f5f5f7;">Yes</strong> → Use CoT. <strong style="color:#f5f5f7;">No</strong> → Standard is enough.',
gui_pill:"06 — Practical Writing Guide",gui_title:"Crafting Effective<br>CoT Prompts.",
gui_1bg:"Technique ①",gui_1t:"Use Clear Instructions",gui_1b:"Rather than simply saying \"step by step,\" specifying the reasoning order and what to do at each step raises the structuring quality of the output.",
gui_1c:'<span class="prompt-label">Prompt Example</span><span class="string">"First organize the problem\'s conditions, then list possible causes,</span><br><span class="string">&nbsp;evaluate the likelihood of each cause, and finally</span><br><span class="string">&nbsp;select the most probable one."</span>',
gui_2bg:"Technique ②",gui_2t:"Combine with Role Setting",gui_2b:"Combining CoT with a Role can induce domain-specific reasoning.",
gui_2c:'<span class="prompt-label">Prompt Example</span><span class="string">"You are a semiconductor back-end quality engineer.</span><br><span class="string">&nbsp;Review the following wire bonding defect data</span><br><span class="string">&nbsp;and analyze the causes step by step."</span>',
gui_3bg:"Technique ③",gui_3t:"Specify Output Format",gui_3b:"To improve readability, explicitly guide the output format of the reasoning process.",
gui_3c:'<span class="prompt-label">Prompt Example</span><span class="string">"Number each step, and for each step separate</span><br><span class="string">&nbsp;\'evidence\' and \'conclusion.\'</span><br><span class="string">&nbsp;At the end, summarize everything in 3 lines."</span>',
gui_4bg:"Technique ④",gui_4t:"Add Self-Verification",gui_4b:"Having the model review its own answer after reasoning makes it one step more accurate.",
gui_4c:'<span class="prompt-label">Prompt Example</span><span class="string">"After completing your answer, check whether</span><br><span class="string">&nbsp;there are contradictions in each step\'s logic,</span><br><span class="string">&nbsp;and correct any errors."</span>',
gui_5bg:"Technique ⑤",gui_5t:"Integrated Application — L&D Example",gui_5b:"A prompt combining all four techniques (Role + Clear Instructions + Format + Self-Verification). Shows a format directly applicable to semiconductor back-end L&D work.",
gui_5c:'<span class="prompt-label">Complete Prompt — Training Module Design (Markdown)</span><span class="md-h1"># Role</span><br><span class="string">"You are a semiconductor back-end training design expert."</span><br><br><span class="md-h2">## Task</span><br><span class="string">"Design a training module on \'Soldering Defect Types and Responses\'</span><br><span class="string">&nbsp;for new engineers."</span><br><br><span class="md-h2">## Steps</span><br><span class="comment">&nbsp;&nbsp;Step 1 —</span> Classify major soldering defect types.<br><span class="comment">&nbsp;&nbsp;Step 2 —</span> Analyze technical causes for each defect type.<br><span class="comment">&nbsp;&nbsp;Step 3 —</span> Derive key training points for each cause.<br><span class="comment">&nbsp;&nbsp;Step 4 —</span> Organize into a 90-minute training session structure.<br><span class="comment">&nbsp;&nbsp;Step 5 —</span> Review overall logical consistency and revise if needed.<br><br><span class="md-h2">## Verification</span><br><span class="string">"Check for any missing content or logical leaps at the end."</span>',
cau_pill:"07 — Limitations & Cautions",cau_title:"It\'s Not a Master Key.",cau_sub:"CoT is powerful but not infallible.<br>You must be aware of several limitations before using it.",
cau_1t:"Self-Reinforcing Bad Reasoning",cau_1b:'If an error occurs at an intermediate step, the model builds subsequent reasoning on that error. <strong style="color:var(--apple-gray-1);">(Confident Hallucination)</strong> can be generated, so <strong style="color:var(--apple-gray-1);">human review must always accompany it</strong>.',
cau_2t:"Reasoning ≠ Understanding",cau_2b:'Step-by-step explanations generated by CoT do not mean the model truly "understands." <strong style="color:var(--apple-gray-1);">Critical review by domain experts is essential</strong>.',
sum_pill:"08 — Key Summary",sum_title:"CoT at a Glance.",sum_1l:"Definition",sum_1b:"A prompting technique that guides AI to describe intermediate reasoning steps toward a conclusion.",sum_2l:"Core Principles",sum_2b:"Problem Decomposition → Intermediate Context Passing → Transparency & Verifiability",sum_rv:"Review",sum_3l:"Main Types",
sum_quote:'"For complex problems, show the thinking process."',sum_close:"CoT ultimately boils down to this single sentence.<br>However, since it\'s not a silver bullet,<br>the real skill is assessing problem complexity first and applying it precisely.<br>Never forget to pair it with human review.",
ftr_title:"Chain of Thought Prompting Handbook · Work Smarter with AI Series 6",ftr_contact:"Contact: L&D Team, Senior Manager Jung Hyuk"
},
vi:{
nav_title:"Sổ tay CoT",nav_def:"Định nghĩa",nav_principle:"Nguyên lý",nav_comparison:"So sánh",nav_types:"Phân loại",nav_usage:"Ứng dụng",nav_guide:"Hướng dẫn",nav_caution:"Lưu ý",nav_summary:"Tóm tắt",
hero_series:"Làm việc thông minh với AI — Tập 6",hero_sub:"Chuỗi Tư duy",hero_tagline:'Kỹ thuật yêu cầu AI thể hiện "quá trình suy nghĩ"',hero_team:"Sổ tay Prompting — Nhóm L&D ATK",hero_btn:"Bắt đầu",
def_pill:"01 — Định nghĩa & Bối cảnh",def_title:"Chain of Thought<br>là gì?",def_subtitle:"Kỹ thuật prompt engineering hướng dẫn mô hình AI mô tả rõ ràng các bước suy luận trung gian để đi đến kết luận, thay vì chỉ đưa ra câu trả lời cuối cùng.",
def_c1t:"Định nghĩa",
def_c1b:'Chain of Thought (Chuỗi Tư duy) là kỹ thuật prompting hướng dẫn LLM tạo ra các bước suy luận trung gian một cách rõ ràng, đạt được cả độ chính xác và tính minh bạch cho các vấn đề phức tạp. <span style="color:var(--apple-blue);font-weight:600;">Điểm mấu chốt không phải là yêu cầu "cho tôi đáp án," mà là "hãy cho tôi thấy bạn đã đi đến đáp án đó như thế nào."</span>',
def_c2t:"Bối cảnh ra đời",
def_c2b:'Năm 2022, Jason Wei và cộng sự tại Google Research đã chính thức đề xuất kỹ thuật này trong bài báo <em>"Chain-of-Thought Prompting Elicits Reasoning in Large Language Models"</em> (NeurIPS 2022). <span style="color:var(--apple-blue);font-weight:600;">Họ đã chứng minh rằng chỉ cần đưa ví dụ về quá trình suy luận vào prompt đã cải thiện đáng kể hiệu suất suy luận số học, logic và thường thức</span>, từ đó xác lập CoT là kỹ thuật cốt lõi trong prompt engineering.',
def_at:"Ví dụ đơn giản",
def_ab:'Giống như yêu cầu <strong style="color:var(--apple-gray-1);">"trình bày cách giải"</strong> trong bài thi toán. Nếu chỉ ghi đáp án, không thể biết sai ở đâu—nhưng trình bày cách giải giúp giảm lỗi và cho phép kiểm tra. Trong quy trình back-end bán dẫn, giống như <strong style="color:var(--apple-gray-1);">theo dõi tỷ lệ đạt ở từng bước quy trình</strong> thay vì chỉ nhìn vào tỷ lệ lỗi cuối cùng.',
pri_pill:"02 — Nguyên lý cốt lõi",pri_title:"Tại sao hiệu quả?",pri_sub:"Hiệu quả của CoT được giải thích bởi ba cơ chế cốt lõi.<br>Mỗi nguyên lý kết hợp hữu cơ để nâng cao độ chính xác suy luận của mô hình.",
pri_f1:"① Phân tách vấn đề",pri_f2:"② Truyền ngữ cảnh",pri_f3:"③ Đảm bảo minh bạch",pri_f4:"Kết luận chính xác",
pri_1t:"Phân tách vấn đề phức tạp",pri_1b:'Chia một vấn đề phức tạp thành nhiều bước con có thể quản lý được. <span style="color:#d1ff26;font-weight:500;">Vì mỗi bước thực hiện một suy luận nhỏ, xác suất lỗi ở mỗi bước giảm đáng kể.</span>',
pri_2t:"Truyền ngữ cảnh trung gian",pri_2b:'Đầu ra của mỗi bước suy luận đóng vai trò là ngữ cảnh cho bước tiếp theo. <span style="color:#d1ff26;font-weight:500;">Mô hình tham chiếu kết luận trước đó khi phát triển logic</span>, tăng tính nhất quán và chặt chẽ tổng thể.',
